      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this is a WGSL thing, seems like it should maybe be done in IrToProgram instead?\n\nWe don\u0027t require this in core Tint IR (we have no behavior analysis to enforce it), and it feels wrong to fixup WGSL-specific things in the SPIR-V frontend.",
      "revId": "b0d63bd63921869e4b7dce93be150e1c3072aa9d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3aa822c0_08b6e3e3",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-09T17:26:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is more a SPIR-V thing as, `unreachable` doesn\u0027t mean `unreachable` in SPIR-V. It just means, undefined behaviour. So, we\u0027re just defining the SPIR-V behaviour. Like, in the examples we have, being `unreachable` seems like an invalid program because it\u0027s obviously reachable.",
      "parentUuid": "ea42df40_eeed4e27",
      "revId": "b0d63bd63921869e4b7dce93be150e1c3072aa9d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cef06e2b_1e995faf",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-09T17:46:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My point is that Tint IR has the same semantics as SPIR-V here. `unreachable` in Tint IR doesn\u0027t mean `unreachable` either. So the translation from SPIR-V to Tint IR is perfectly correct.\n\nAll of the other textual backends handle this case in their respective printers, so it makes sense to me that we do the same in WGSL.",
      "parentUuid": "3aa822c0_08b6e3e3",
      "revId": "b0d63bd63921869e4b7dce93be150e1c3072aa9d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
